After playing on and off for nigh on fifteen years, I've finally done
it!

Can't really say with any surety what happened over the course of the
game.  Met a lot of wraiths, ten of which left fully-edible corpses.
Nothing too memorable happened over the course of the game - I played
extremely carefully and tramped up, down, left, right and all 'round
the dungeons quite a few times searching for items to round out my
ascension kit.  As it was, I ended up extremely short of food

Oh- it was the only time Grayswandir hasn't eluded my grasp when I've
wished for it.  Probably the only notable thing that happened in the
game.  Everything else was pretty run-of-the-mill, at least I would
assume.  I ended up not taking a whole lot of notes this game,
preferring to concentrate on not dying.

In my haste I forgot to grab a few scrolls of gold detection I'd
stashed.  I had a few spells I'd forgotten by that point that would
have made it pretty easy to find the portals on the planes.  As it
was, I had to zap and zap and zap my only wand of secret door
detection and pray to Odin that I was in the right spot.  I ended up
stumbling upon the portal in the plane of Water fairly quickly, which
was a godsend.  Otherwise, I think I would have starved.  Didn't find
a whole lot of food to bring with me.

Also, I lucked out in that the first altar I came to was my own.
Otherwise I would've been toast.

Ah well.  An ascension is an ascension.  I'm not going to complain
about the little details.

Whew.

